To find $h'(x)$, we will need to use the product rule *and* the chain rule!

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}h'(x)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[u(x)\cdot v\Bigl(w(x)\Bigr)\right]
\\\\
&=u'(x)\cdot v\Bigl(w(x)\Bigr)+u(x)\cdot\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[v\Bigl(w(x)\Bigr)\right]\quad\gray{\text{Product rule}}
\\\\
&=u'(x)\cdot v\Bigl(w(x)\Bigr)+u(x)\cdot v'\Bigl(w(x)\Bigr)\cdot w'(x)\quad\gray{\text{Chain rule}}
\end{align}$
